<title>USA: Fannie Mae to redeem $750 mln in issues.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae to redeem $750 mln in issues.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fannie Mae on Monday said it will redeem all outstanding amounts of one debenture issue totalling $500 million and two medium-term notes totalling $250 million as follows.</p>
<p>DEBENTURE ISSUE:</p>
<p>    Principal   Rate    Maturity    Cusip    Redemption</p>
<p>  $500 million  7.65    04/29/04  31359CAR6  06/11/97</p>
<p>MEDIUM-TERM NOTES:</p>
<p>    Principal   Rate    Maturity    Cusip    Redemption</p>
<p>  $150 million  7.64    06/16/04  31364AW24  06/16/97</p>
<p>  $100 million  7.26    05/16/00  31364BCS7  06/16/97</p>
<p>The debenture issue has series number SM-2004-E. The redemption price of the debenture and notes will be 100 percent of the principal amount plus interest accrued to the redemption date, Fannie Mae said.</p>
</text>
